    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d512">

                <pb facs="0472" n="462" xml:id="pg462"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/1905: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The First Secretary of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-07T16:00:00+08:00">January 7, 1941—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>14. Reference first paragraph of Peiping’s 10, January 5, 5 p.m.,<anchor n="13"
                        xml:id="d512-f1"/> marine-gendarme incident. Colonel Turnage has received a
                    message from Admiral Hart expressing thorough approval of the position adopted
                    by him as well as his handling of the matter; the Admiral added that in view of
                    the unreasonable and difficult attitude adopted by the Japanese he desired that
                    Colonel Turnage should confine further negotiations to receiving Japanese
                    amends.</p>
                <p>Colonel Turnage states that Admiral Hart has reported to the Navy Department that
                    the matter has reached an impasse and that he (Admiral Hart) considers the
                    conduct of the Japanese so flagrant that the United States Government should
                    take strong measures to obtain redress.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Departments Repeated to Chungking, Tokyo, Shanghai.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smyth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
